# =============================================================================
# Docker build context
# =============================================================================
# The context is the repository root, because the Airflow image copies dags/
# and docker/airflow/requirements.txt from different places in the tree.
#
# Without this file the context is ~2.9 GB, almost all of it Terraform provider
# binaries under .terraform/. Both build paths tar and upload the whole context
# before the first layer runs, so the effect is a build that appears to hang for
# ten minutes and then transfers 2.9 GB. With this file the context is under a
# megabyte.
# =============================================================================

# Terraform — provider binaries, state, plans
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/tfplan
**/backend.hcl
**/*.tfvars

# Version control
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Nothing below is needed to build or run Airflow
docs/
kubernetes/
scripts/
azure-pipelines/
policies/
terraform/
Makefile
README.md
*.md

# Python and OS noise
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
